       message) may break those services' rules. Such features are off by default and you use them at your
       own risk. The Author is not responsible for warnings, kicks or bans by third parties.

6. Updates and pre-release versions
   6.1 HAULIX checks for new versions and can update itself with your confirmation. You can turn the update
       check off in the settings. Updates may add, change or remove features.
   6.2 Versions marked "BETA", "DEVKIT" or similar are pre-release software. They may contain errors and
       features that are unfinished, not yet available or not final.

7. Your data
   HAULIX stores your logbook, settings and backups only on your PC. How HAULIX handles data, including the
   future online services, is described in the HAULIX Privacy Policy (PRIVACY), which is part of this
   agreement.


PART B – HAULIX ONLINE SERVICES

The following applies as soon as online features are available (for example accounts, finding and joining
VTCs, company pages, events and convoys, job board, leaderboards and cloud sync – the "Online Services").
Online Services are always optional; HAULIX keeps working offline without them.

8. Account
   8.1 To use Online Services you may need to sign in with a supported account (for example Discord or
       Steam). You must be at least 16 years old, or have permission from a parent or guardian.
   8.2 Keep your account secure. You are responsible for what happens with your account. Tell the Author
       without delay if you believe your account has been misused.
   8.3 One person, one account. Accounts may not be sold, shared or transferred.

9. Your content
   9.1 "Your Content" is anything you create or upload through the Online Services: profile and company
       names, descriptions, logos, messages, events, jobs and uploaded delivery data.
   9.2 You keep all rights in Your Content. You give the Author a free, worldwide, non-exclusive licence to
       store, process, display and share Your Content as far as necessary to run, show and improve the Online
       Services (for example showing your company page to other users or your results on a leaderboard).
       This licence ends when you delete Your Content or your account, except for copies in backups for a
       limited time and content that other users already shared with your permission.
   9.3 You confirm that you have the rights to Your Content and that it does not break the law or the rights
       of others.

10. Conduct
    You may not use the Online Services to:
    a) harass, threaten, insult or discriminate against others, or post hateful, violent, sexual or illegal
       content;
    b) impersonate other people, VTCs or companies, or mislead others about your identity;
    c) send spam or advertising, or recruit for other services in a way that disturbs others;
    d) manipulate leaderboards, statistics or deliveries (for example with fake telemetry, edited data,
       cheats or automation);
    e) attack, overload, scan or reverse engineer the Online Services or access them with unofficial tools,
       bots or scrapers;
    f) collect personal data of other users.

11. Moderation, suspension and termination
    11.1 The Author may remove content, reset manipulated statistics, and warn, suspend or close accounts that
         break this agreement, the law or the rights of others. Where reasonable, you will be told why and can
         object.
    11.2 You can stop using the Online Services and delete your account at any time.
    11.3 The Author may change, pause or end Online Services or individual features, for example for
         maintenance, security or because a service is discontinued. Where possible, this will be announced
         in advance, and you will be able to export your data first.

12. Availability and cost
    12.1 The Online Services are currently free. Should paid features ever be offered, they will be clearly
         marked and require your separate agreement; nothing will be charged without it.
    12.2 There is no guarantee that the Online Services are always available, error-free or secure against
         all attacks. Your local logbook in HAULIX is not affected by outages.


PART C – GENERAL

13. Warranty and liability
    13.1 HAULIX and the Online Services are provided free of charge and "as is". The Author gives no warranty
         that they are free of errors or suitable for a particular purpose. Make backups of important data.
    13.2 The Author is liable without limitation for intent and gross negligence, for injury to life, body or
         health, under the German Product Liability Act and where a guarantee was given. For free software,
         liability for simple negligence is excluded as far as the law allows (§§ 521, 599 German Civil Code).
    13.3 Mandatory rights you have as a consumer under the law of your country remain unaffected.

14. Termination
    This licence ends automatically if you break this agreement. You must then uninstall HAULIX and delete all
    copies. Sections 2 to 5, 9.2 (for content already shared), 13 and 15 continue to apply.

15. Changes to this agreement
    The Author may update this agreement, for example when new features or Online Services are added. The
    current version is shown in the installer and in HAULIX (Settings → About). For changes that matter to
    you, you will be asked to accept the new version when you install an update or use the Online Services.

16. Law and final provisions
    16.1 German law applies, excluding the UN Convention on Contracts for the International Sale of Goods. If
         you are a consumer, this choice does not take away the protection of mandatory law of the country
         where you live.
    16.2 If a provision of this agreement is invalid, the rest remains valid.
    16.3 The HAULIX Privacy Policy (PRIVACY) and the third-party notices (THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES) are part of this
         agreement.

